VERDICT: THE EXTREMALITY IS VACUOUS, SO BOTH HALVES OF THE LEMMA FAIL.

  The infimum of delta is 0 at EVERY g from 1 to 6, not only at g >= 4. So
      inf over g >= 4  =  inf over g = 4
  is true, but it reads 0 = 0, and "permitting more intervening moves cannot produce a
  shallower returning setter" is true only because nothing can go below zero anywhere.

  The apparent extremality in the first run was SAMPLING NOISE. Bin sizes there were 39, 95,
  173, 76 and 21, and the minima were 3.7e-03, 1.8e-04, 1.7e-03, 1.1e-04, 8.6e-04 -- all
  within an order of magnitude. g = 4 held the lowest draw; that is all it was.

  HOW THIS WAS NEARLY MISSED, twice over. A first attempt used 150 random restarts per g.
  A g = 4 return occurs in about 0.4% of random arrangements, so that expects under one hit,
  and it duly reported "none found" for five of the six values of g -- a null manufactured by
  an underpowered search. Harvesting seeds first (69,341 arrangements scanned, 25 per g) and
  refining those gives the table above.

  NOTE THE DIRECTION. Today's other underpowered searches manufactured NULLS. This one
  manufactured a POSITIVE: an apparent structural fact, g = 4 being extremal, that was an
  artefact of bin sizes. The same defect, opposite sign.

WHERE THE LEMMA NOW STANDS
  c_* > 0                     refuted -- delta reaches 6.1e-13 on an arriving cascade
  extremality at g = 4        vacuous -- every infimum is 0
  would a true floor help?    no -- log growth ~ (1/4 - delta)/N, and convergence is governed
                              by sum 1/N_j, which a constant floor does not touch
